# PROJECT SPECIFICATION: RRB NOTICE MONITOR — FRESH PRODUCTION BUILD

## 1. ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior full-stack TypeScript engineer, web-scraping specialist, test engineer, database architect, and Telegram automation developer.

Build a completely new, production-oriented Railway Recruitment Board (RRB) official-notice monitoring system from scratch.

Primary official website:
https://rrb.indianrailways.gov.in/

The system must monitor all discoverable regional Railway Recruitment Boards and all relevant notice categories on the unified official portal.

The production system must:
- Run automatically every 10 minutes through cron-job.org.
- Fetch and parse official RRB notices.
- Identify genuinely new notices.
- Send only eligible new notices to a Telegram bot.
- Store notice fingerprints, delivery status, history, and baseline information persistently in GitHub.
- Never resend a previously delivered notice during normal operation.
- Never send existing historical notices as new notices during initial setup.
- Provide an all-zones test that verifies every configured board and reports the actual latest notice discovered for each board.
- Provide safe recovery from network failures, parser failures, state-write conflicts, Telegram errors, and interrupted executions.

Do not reuse code, configuration, deployment settings, state files, credentials, or assumptions from any older scraper project. Create an independent implementation with its own repository, configuration, state namespace, tests, and documentation.

Do not claim that the application is production-ready until its tests have actually run and the implementation satisfies the acceptance criteria below.

