## 7. INITIAL BASELINE — ABSOLUTELY NO HISTORICAL ALERTS

The first production initialization must operate in baseline-only mode.

Procedure:

1. Discover all configured boards.
2. Fetch their notice listings and required pages.
3. Parse and validate the discovered notices.
4. Record existing notice fingerprints and publication dates.
5. Persist the initial baseline.
6. Confirm that all required boards have been accounted for.
7. Mark the baseline as complete only after the required baseline state has been successfully persisted.

Do not send individual historical notices to Telegram during baseline creation.

Do not mark the baseline complete after a partial scan or a failed state write.

If some boards fail, persist their error statuses and use an explicit resumable initialization process. Do not silently establish an incomplete baseline.

Before enabling production delivery, require a successful baseline and an explicit operational readiness check.

After baseline initialization, only newly observed, valid notices that meet the new-notice eligibility rules may enter the production delivery queue.

If a board was unavailable during baseline creation, treat its first successful scan carefully. Do not automatically send all historical items discovered on recovery as new. Baseline that board first unless trustworthy publication and prior-state evidence establishes genuine novelty.

Provide a documented administrative reset procedure. A reset must require explicit authorization, display its consequences, and never silently clear historical fingerprints.

## 8. NEW-NOTICE ELIGIBILITY

A notice is eligible for a new-alert message only when all of these conditions are satisfied:

- The baseline is complete.
- The notice came from a verified official source.
- The notice has a valid, deterministic fingerprint.
- The notice is not already in the persistent notice history.
- The notice is not already pending, sending, delivered, or uncertain in the delivery queue.
- The notice is not classified as a historical item discovered during recovery.
- Its publication metadata and source evidence have passed the configured validation rules.
- The state store is healthy and safe to update.
- No conflicting scan or delivery operation owns the relevant lock.

Distinguish a genuinely new notice from an old notice that has just appeared on another board, moved to the top of a list, been exposed through pagination, or been found after a previous fetch failure.

When publication dates are available, compare them with stored history and first-seen evidence. When publication dates are missing or unreliable, use a conservative policy and do not claim that the publication is new merely because it is newly discovered.

If a new official notice has an older publication date, do not automatically discard it forever. Record it for review or quarantine unless trustworthy evidence shows that it is genuinely new. Make the policy configurable and explain its effect in the dashboard and documentation.

A new corrigendum or revised official document may deserve a new alert if it has a distinct official identity or a validated new version. Do not resend an unchanged document.

## 9. TELEGRAM MESSAGE FORMAT

Use the Telegram Bot API from server-side code.

Example format:

🚆 NEW RRB OFFICIAL NOTICE

Board: {boardName}
Category: {category}
Title: {title}
Publication Date: {publicationDate}

Official Notice:
{officialNoticeUrl}

PDF / Attachment:
{attachmentUrlIfAvailable}

Detected At: {detectedAtIST}

The format is an example; populate it exclusively from validated notice data.

Requirements:
- Send only eligible new notices in production mode.
- Include the board name and official source link.
- Escape HTML or Markdown correctly according to the selected Telegram parse mode.
- Respect Telegram message-length limits.
- Split long text safely if required.
- Handle HTTP errors, API-level errors, rate limits, and Retry-After instructions.
- Never expose bot tokens in URLs printed to logs.
- Do not send the same notice separately for duplicate listings across boards.
- Preserve the original board attribution and all relevant official links.
- Do not generate artificial notices to simulate successful scraping.

Implement a global delivery queue with persistent statuses:
discovered, pending, sending, sent, failed, and uncertain.

Use an atomic claim or durable lock before delivery.

Persist the delivery intent before sending and persist the Telegram message ID and successful delivery result when available.

Acknowledge that Telegram does not provide a general idempotency key for sendMessage. If the request times out after Telegram may have accepted the message, use an uncertain-delivery state and reconciliation policy rather than blindly retrying forever.

Prioritize avoiding duplicate alerts. Provide controlled retries, manual reconciliation, and an auditable history of every delivery attempt.

